text:
The same annotation, three formats



COCO · one JSON file for the whole dataset


amcr-pas_v0.json

{"id": 9872, "image_id": 8987, "category_id": 58,
 "bbox": [837.8, 1760.0, 485.2, 445.9],
 "segmentation": [[1301.3, 1762.7, 1279.0, 1760.0, …]]}

bbox is the top-left corner plus width and height, in pixels. The polygon is kept. The image and the class name are found only by id.


YOLO · one .txt per image, one line per object


labels/M202400071N00083F01.txt

57 0.271594 0.717940 0.121971 0.161441



data.yaml

names: {…, 57: cross, …}

Class, then centre x, y, width, height ÷ image size. 0-based, so 58 becomes 57; cross is only in data.yaml. The polygon is gone.



Pascal VOC · one .xml per image


Annotations/M202400071N00083F01.xml

&lt;annotation&gt;
  &lt;filename&gt;M202400071N00083F01.jpeg&lt;/filename&gt;
  &lt;size&gt;&lt;width&gt;3978&lt;/width&gt; &lt;height&gt;2762&lt;/height&gt;&lt;/size&gt;
  &lt;object&gt;
    &lt;name&gt;cross&lt;/name&gt;
    &lt;bndbox&gt;
      &lt;xmin&gt;838&lt;/xmin&gt; &lt;ymin&gt;1760&lt;/ymin&gt;
      &lt;xmax&gt;1323&lt;/xmax&gt; &lt;ymax&gt;2206&lt;/ymax&gt;
    &lt;/bndbox&gt;
  &lt;/object&gt;
&lt;/annotation&gt;

The box is two corners, in whole pixels. The class name is written out, and the file names its own image. The polygon is gone.









Important


Every conversion is lossy in a different direction — and 57 means nothing without the data.yaml it came with.





If time is short, skip VOC and compare the two blocks on the left — the normalisation and the lost class name are the two things worth their slide space.
YOLO also has a segmentation variant that keeps polygons (normalised x y pairs after the class), so “the polygon is gone” is true of the detection format shown here.

The mapping, as a file
@prefix skos: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#&gt; .
@prefix fish: &lt;http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/mda_obj/concepts/&gt; .
@prefix amcr: &lt;https://example.org/amcr-pas/&gt; .    # placeholder, see below

fish:96665   skos:prefLabel    "Brooch"@en ;
             skos:exactMatch   amcr:fibula .

fish:140465  skos:prefLabel    "Strap end"@en ;
             skos:exactMatch   amcr:mordant .

fish:97525   skos:prefLabel    "Coin hoard"@en ;
             skos:narrowMatch  amcr:coin .

fish:95426   skos:prefLabel    "Jetton"@en ;
             skos:relatedMatch amcr:coin .



One row of the sheet is one triple — Turtle, the W3C text format for RDF
fish: URIs are the FISH thesaurus’ own; amcr: is a placeholder — the sheet has AMČR-PAS labels, not URIs
validated has no SKOS predicate: 388 of 841 rows are unchecked, so publish the checked ones, or say who checked what




Four rows straight from the mapping sheet (fish column → subject, mappingRelation → predicate, target → object). Point out that the file is readable without any tooling — that is the argument for publishing it next to the dataset. The real AMČR-PAS concept URIs replace the placeholder once the categories are published.
